- [Press Conference by Prime Minister Kishida](https://japan.kantei.go.jp/101_kishida/statement/202204/_00012.html) - Prime Minister’s Office of Japan, 2022-04. Kishida said the government would lower the gasoline benchmark price to 168 yen near term, raise the subsidy cap, and expand support to sectors hit by fuel costs. Useful as a specific household/business shock-relief measure. Temporal fit: spring 2022 inflation pressure. Ruler attribution: direct Kishida policy choice. Contrary points: fuel subsidies are stabilizing but not structurally transformative. Lenses: 5B.3, 5B.9, 5B.10.
