- [IMF Executive Board Concludes 2022 Article IV Consultation with Japan](https://www.imf.org/en/news/articles/2022/04/06/pr22106-imf-executive-board-concludes-2022-article-iv-consultation-with-japan) - IMF, 2022-04-06. The IMF projected 2022 real GDP growth of 2.4 percent, inflation of 1.0 percent, and low unemployment under continued policy support, while warning that commodity prices and the Ukraine conflict would slow domestic demand. This is baseline-plus-constraint context, not a pure Kishida credit item. Temporal fit: early 2022 macro outlook. Ruler attribution: partly inherited and partly policy-supported. Contrary points: forecast, not realized outcome; does not show Kishida uniquely caused the numbers. Lenses: 5B.3, 5B.9, 5B.10.
