- [Japan Inc hikes pay by more than 2%, not enough for a big economic boost](https://www.investing.com/news/economy/japan-inc-expected-to-announce-modest-wage-hikes-after-annual-talks-2785386) - Reuters via Investing.com, 2022-03-15. Top firms offered pay rises above 2% but still below Kishida’s request for 3%+; the article also notes higher food and fuel prices would offset much of the benefit. Useful as both evidence of pressure and a limit on results. Temporal fit: spring 2022 wage round. Ruler attribution: Kishida’s public pressure helped shape the wage debate, though firms made the actual decisions. Contrary points: outcome was modest and not enough for a broad boost. Lenses: 5B.1, 5B.7, 5B.8, 5B.10.
