- [Japan's planned record minimum wage hike opens path to sustained GDP growth](https://www.investing.com/news/economy/japans-average-minimum-wage-set-to-rise-at-record-pace-this-year-nikkei-2859912) - Reuters via Investing.com, 2022-08-01. Japan’s average minimum wage was approved to rise by 31 yen, or a record 3.3%, to 961 yen per hour, and Reuters said Kishida was counting on it to support broader wealth distribution and recovery. This is a concrete income-side policy. Temporal fit: 2022 wage-setting. Ruler attribution: direct Kishida policy environment, though implementation uses ministry process. Contrary points: benefits are gradual and not enough alone to shift the whole economy. Lenses: 5B.1, 5B.3, 5B.8, 5B.10.
