- [Press Conference by Prime Minister Kishida](https://japan.kantei.go.jp/101_kishida/statement/202210/_00023.html) - Prime Minister’s Office of Japan, 2022-10-28. Kishida announced a 72 trillion yen package with 39 trillion yen in fiscal spending, estimated GDP boost of 4.6 percent, consumer-price reduction over 1.2 percent, 20 percent lower electricity fees, 45,000 yen average household aid, support for SMEs, tourism, and 1 trillion yen over five years for people investment. This is the central fiscal-economy item of 2022. Temporal fit: late-2022 response to inflation and the weak yen. Ruler attribution: direct Kishida cabinet choice. Contrary points: this is a large fiscal cushion, but it also signals a heavy subsidy approach and depends on future execution. Lenses: 5B.3, 5B.6, 5B.8, 5B.9, 5B.10.
