- [Press Conference by Prime Minister Kishida](https://japan.kantei.go.jp/101_kishida/statement/202212/_00004.html) - Prime Minister’s Office of Japan, 2022-12-10. Kishida said the average household would receive 47,000 yen of aid, continued business support for energy bills, and a child-support package with 100,000 yen in flexible support plus a record increase in childbirth allowance to 500,000 yen. This shows distributional and family-oriented spending. Temporal fit: year-end implementation. Ruler attribution: direct Kishida choice. Contrary points: these are support measures, not evidence that wages already outpaced prices. Lenses: 5B.6, 5B.8, 5B.9, 5B.10.
