- [Press Conference by Prime Minister Kishida](https://japan.kantei.go.jp/101_kishida/statement/202212/_00006.html) - Prime Minister’s Office of Japan, 2022-12-16. Kishida’s ruling parties proposed a corporate surtax of 4.0-4.5 percent with SME exemptions, and he said they would not increase the income-tax burden while securing stable revenue. Useful for fiscal-credibility and fairness. Temporal fit: late-2022 tax reform. Ruler attribution: direct Kishida-led tax policy. Contrary points: raising corporate taxes can also be read as a burden shift rather than pure growth policy. Lenses: 5B.3, 5B.4, 5B.5, 5B.7.
