- [Japan's inflation hits 40-year high as BOJ sticks to easy policy](https://www.investing.com/news/economy/japans-inflation-hits-40year-high-as-boj-sticks-to-easy-policy-2947396) - Reuters via Investing.com, 2022-11-17. Japan’s core CPI rose 3.6 percent in October, a 40-year high, driven by yen weakness and imported-cost pressures while the BOJ kept policy easy. This is key macro context and a major constraint on Kishida’s stewardship. Temporal fit: late 2022 inflation shock. Ruler attribution: not directly Kishida-controlled because monetary policy was BOJ-run, but it shaped his fiscal response. Contrary points: inflation was external-cost driven, so not purely a policy failure. Lenses: 5B.3, 5B.9, 5B.10.
