- [Japan’s workers get biggest pay rises in decades as inflation surges](https://www.investing.com/news/economy/japans-big-firms-set-to-offer-biggest-pay-rises-in-decades-3030602) - Reuters via Investing.com, 2023-03, describing 2022 wage trajectory and Kishida’s agenda. Reuters reported that pay rises in the 2022 spring wage round were still only modest and that Kishida’s call for higher pay was set against inflation and weak real income. This is a useful negative/comparison item for the 2022 trajectory. Temporal fit: retrospective on 2022 wage outcomes. Ruler attribution: Kishida influenced the policy climate but not the company wage offers. Contrary points: it underscores that pay growth lagged prices. Lenses: 5B.1, 5B.7, 5B.8, 5B.10.
