- [Japan: 2022 Article IV Consultation-Press Release; Staff Report; and Statement by the Executive Director for Japan](https://www.imf.org/en/publications/cr/issues/2022/04/06/japan-2022-article-iv-consultation-press-release-staff-report-and-statement-by-the-516216) - IMF, 2022-04-06. The IMF said domestic demand was recovering, but higher commodity prices and the Ukraine conflict would slow it; it also emphasized that fiscal buffers should be rebuilt gradually and structural reforms should raise potential growth. This is a useful independent check on the constraints Kishida faced and the direction needed. Temporal fit: 2022 surveillance. Ruler attribution: partly inherited macro structure, partly Kishida’s policy domain. Contrary points: it is advice and context, not a result evaluation. Lenses: 5B.3, 5B.7, 5B.9, 5B.10.
